{{also|Tauchen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|gmh|tūchen}}, {{m|gmh|touchen}}, from {{der|de|goh||-tūhhan}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*dūkaną}}. Cognate to {{cog|nl|duiken}}. The word had become obsolete in [[Upper German]], but was later reintroduced on the basis of [[Central German]] {{m|gmh||dūchen, tūchen}} and {{der|de|gml|dūken}}, which had remained common. In the course of this process, the originally strong verb became weak. A derivative with [[Low German]] consonantism is {{m|de|ducken}} (cognate to and synonymous with {{cog|en|duck}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈtaʊ̯xən/|[ˈtaʊ̯xən]|[ˈtaʊ̯xn̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-tauchen.ogg|Audio}}
* {{hyphenation|de|tau|chen}}

